{
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;text-align:justify;mso-layout-grid-align:none;\r\ntext-autospace:none&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:&amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;,sans-serif&quot;&gt;The proposed boundary\r\ntreatment comprising vehicle and pedestrian gate, iron railing and brick pillar,\r\nby reason of their unacceptable height inappropriate urban design and inappropriate\r\nrelationship with the public realm,, appears as an incongruous and visually\r\nobtrusive addition to the street scene out of keeping with the character of the\r\nlocal area, and there is not clear and convincing justification for the harm,\r\nnor public benefits to outweigh them. Therefore the proposed boundary treatment\r\n&amp;nbsp;is harmful to the character and\r\nappearance of the area and contrary to the high quality design aspirations of\r\nthe National Planning Policy Framework (2024), policies D3.D(1) and D3.D(11) of\r\nThe London Plan (2021), policies CS1.B of the Harrow Core Strategy (2012),\r\npolicy DM1 of the Development Management Policies Local Plan 2013 and the\r\nSupplementary Planning Document: Residential Design Guide (2010).&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
